<p id="Ch0.S9.SS2.tab1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Parameter combinations of the fundamental Planck scale <math id="Ch0.S9.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\text{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\text{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> and minimum black hole mass <math id="Ch0.S9.SS2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\text{BH}}^{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mtext>BH</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\text{BH}}^{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> (both in <span id="Ch0.S9.SS2.tab1.2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\TeV</span>) that exclude a given number of extra dimensions <math id="Ch0.S9.SS2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for BH models generated with <span id="Ch0.S9.SS2.tab1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BlackMax</span> and <span id="Ch0.S9.SS2.tab1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Charybdis2</span>. Each row collects all (<math id="Ch0.S9.SS2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\text{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\text{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ch0.S9.SS2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\text{BH}}^{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mtext>BH</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\text{BH}}^{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>) pairs yielding the same exclusion level. Combinations with <math id="Ch0.S9.SS2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\text{BH}}^{\text{min}}&lt;M_{\text{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mtext>BH</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mtext>D</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\text{BH}}^{\text{min}}&lt;M_{\text{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> are unphysical and not considered. The first row indicates the pairs that are excluded for any number of extra dimensions in the ADD model, while the last row shows the parameters where no exclusion could be made in this analysis.



